--- answer ---
Found it. `Resize` uses `i <= diff` in the loop, so it removes `diff+1` entries instead of `diff`. When `size` equals the current length, `diff` is 0 and it still evicts one entry.Fixed `simplelru.Resize`: changed the eviction loop from `i <= diff` to `i < diff` so it evicts exactly `diff` entries instead of one extra. Build, vet, and tests pass.